{"step_index":164,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-04T21:56:13Z","thinking":"**Discovering Outlier Scores**\n\nI've made a breakthrough! I've spotted the outlier score computed by vidIQ directly within the DOM. I am examining specific lines within the code that appear to contain the score. It's a key piece of data now in sight! I'll investigate lines 4, 5, 22, 25, 44, and 45 for more data.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import re\nfrom bs4 import BeautifulSoup\n\nhtml_path = r\"C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\New folder\\YouTube.html\"\nout_path = r\"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\7a78deb3-fd50-47e2-8d2a-a23cba5ad928\\youtube_videos.md\"\n\ndef parse_score(text):\n    text = text.replace('x', '').replace('>', '').strip()\n    try:\n        if text == '100': return 100.0 # for >100x\n        return float(text)\n    except:\n        return 0.0\n\nwith open(html_path, 'r', encoding='utf-8', errors='ignore') as f:\n    soup = BeautifulSoup(f, 'html.parser')\n\nresults = []\n\n# Find all video renderers\nrenderers = soup.find_all(['ytd-rich-item-renderer', 'ytd-rich-grid-media', 'ytd-video-renderer'])\n\nfor renderer in renderers:\n    title_elem = renderer.find(id='video-title')\n    if not title_elem:\n        title_elem = renderer.find('h3')\n        \n    title = title_elem.text.strip() if title_elem else \"\"\n    if not title:\n        continue\n        \n    # Search for outlier score e.g., \"5.7x\" or \">100x\" inside a span or a\n    outlier_text = \"N/A\"\n    outlier_val = -1.0\n    \n    # Try finding the outlier score span (vidiq classes or ends with 'x')\n    for elem in renderer.find_all(['span', 'a']):\n        text = elem.text.strip()\n        if re.match(r'^(>)?\\d+(\\.\\d+)?x$', text):\n            outlier_text = text\n            outlier_val = parse_score(text)\n            break\n            \n    # Also get views if possible\n    views_elem = renderer.find(string=re.compile(r'views', re.IGNORECASE))\n    views_text = views_elem.strip() if views_elem else \"\"\n\n    title_clean = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', title)\n    \n    # Only add if it hasn't been added with a better score\n    existing = next((i for i, r in enumerate(results) if r['title'] == title_clean), -1)\n    if existing >= 0:\n        if outlier_val > results[existing]['score']:\n            results[existing] = {'title': title_clean, 'score': outlier_val, 'score_text': outlier_text, 'views': views_text}\n    else:\n        results.append({\n            'title': title_clean, \n            'score': outlier_val,\n            'score_text': outlier_text,\n            'views': views_text\n        })\n\n# Sort decreasing\nresults.sort(key=lambda x: x['score'], reverse=True)\n\nmd = \"# All YouTube Videos (Sorted by Outlier Score)\\n\\n\"\nmd += \"*I have extracted the outlier scores directly from the vidIQ elements embedded in your saved HTML file. Videos without a score are listed at the bottom.* \\n\\n\"\n\nfor r in results:\n    md += f\"### {r['title']}\\n\"\n    if r['score_text'] != 'N/A':\n        md += f\"- **Outlier Score:** {r['score_text']}\\n\"\n    if r['views']:\n        md += f\"- **Views:** {r['views']}\\n\"\n    md += \"\\n\"\n\nwith open(out_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    f.write(md)\n\nprint(f\"Successfully processed {len(results)} videos and wrote to {out_path}\")\n","Description":"Extract outlier scores from DOM.","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\extract_vidiq.py","toolAction":"Creating DOM extraction script","toolSummary":"Write outlier score extraction script"}}]}
